WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.149 --> 00:00:03.940
Hello, and welcome to Healthcare
Information Systems.

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.439
I'm Dr.

3
00:00:05.439 --> 00:00:07.412
Brad Trinkle, and I'll be your
instructor this semester.

4
00:00:07.412 --> 00:00:11.847
This course is about the decisions healthcare
leaders make about information

5
00:00:11.847 --> 00:00:13.068
systems.

6
00:00:13.068 --> 00:00:18.239
The technical background you need is what you
learned in your prerequisite MIS

7
00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:18.839
course, MIS 3010.

8
00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:22.953
You will learn how information systems
support patient care and hospital

9
00:00:22.953 --> 00:00:26.123
operations, and how to lead people
through a major system change.

10
00:00:26.123 --> 00:00:29.586
You will also learn to use AI the way a
healthcare leader should: to work faster

11
00:00:29.586 --> 00:00:34.831
and think more clearly, while you check what
it gives you and keep the judgment

12
00:00:34.831 --> 00:00:36.542
calls your own.

13
00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:37.974
Here is how the course works.

14
00:00:37.974 --> 00:00:42.598
It is online and asynchronous, so there
are no live class meetings.

15
00:00:42.598 --> 00:00:44.034
The whole course is one story.

16
00:00:44.034 --> 00:00:48.542
You are the new Assistant to the Chief of
Staff at Kestrel Falls Community

17
00:00:48.542 --> 00:00:52.064
Hospital, or KFCH, a fictional
community hospital in Iowa.

18
00:00:52.064 --> 00:00:56.874
KFCH has just learned that the company behind
its electronic health record will

19
00:00:56.874 --> 00:00:59.830
stop supporting it in about two years.

20
00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.435
Your mentor, Laura Hemmingsen,
the Chief of Staff,

21
00:01:01.435 --> 00:01:06.441
brings you onto the team that will choose a
new EHR and plan the switch.

22
00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:10.191
Along the way you will hear from doctors,
nurses, IT staff, patients, and families,

23
00:01:10.191 --> 00:01:13.640
each with their own worries
about the change.

24
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.346
At the end of the semester, you present your
recommendation to the KFCH board.

25
00:01:18.346 --> 00:01:19.682
A quick note about the videos.

26
00:01:19.682 --> 00:01:23.547
The weekly lectures are presented by an
AI-generated avatar of me,

27
00:01:23.547 --> 00:01:26.512
and the KFCH people you interview are
AI-generated avatars too.

28
00:01:26.512 --> 00:01:28.177
Every one of them is labeled.

29
00:01:28.177 --> 00:01:31.564
I developed the course with the
assistance of my AI team,

30
00:01:31.564 --> 00:01:36.257
and the real-world facts in each lecture come
from the sources listed in its

31
00:01:36.257 --> 00:01:37.459
transcript.

32
00:01:37.459 --> 00:01:40.107
Each module follows the same eight
steps: the problem lands,

33
00:01:40.107 --> 00:01:44.717
you learn from a video lecture, you make
your own first call without AI,

34
00:01:44.717 --> 00:01:47.138
you practice with Copilot, you
build the deliverable,

35
00:01:47.138 --> 00:01:50.493
you get feedback from your AI
coach and revise,

36
00:01:50.493 --> 00:01:56.474
you work through an ethics exercise, and
you write a short reflection.

37
00:01:56.474 --> 00:01:59.191
Most modules take one week; Modules
4, 5, and 12 take two.

38
00:01:59.191 --> 00:02:01.886
Expect about six hours of work a week.

39
00:02:01.886 --> 00:02:05.651
AI is part of the course, about a
fifth of the hands-on work,

40
00:02:05.651 --> 00:02:08.566
but the focus is your judgment as
a healthcare leader.

41
00:02:08.566 --> 00:02:12.688
For AI, you use Microsoft Copilot through a
Microsoft 365 Personal plan,

42
00:02:12.688 --> 00:02:16.262
which Microsoft discounts for
college students.

43
00:02:16.262 --> 00:02:20.058
You set it up, along with your AI coach,
in the Start Here module.

44
00:02:20.058 --> 00:02:23.602
Please read the Course Technology page
before the semester starts.

45
00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:28.190
The step-by-step walkthroughs, data files, and
videos are on the course website.

46
00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:31.978
You will find the link on each module's
overview page in Canvas.

47
00:02:31.978 --> 00:02:35.434
When you finish a module, the website
builds your Word document,

48
00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.272
and you upload it in Canvas.

49
00:02:37.272 --> 00:02:39.056
There is no final exam.

50
00:02:39.056 --> 00:02:43.656
In the final week, you record your board
presentation in Canvas Studio instead.

51
00:02:43.656 --> 00:02:45.405
One important thing about the website.

52
00:02:45.405 --> 00:02:49.401
Use Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge on a
computer for this course.

53
00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:52.019
What you type on the website is
kept in that browser,

54
00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:53.996
so the first time you open a module,

55
00:02:53.996 --> 00:02:59.810
click the button at the bottom left of the page
that says Turn on automatic saving.

56
00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.963
Pick a folder you will not
delete, and click Save.

57
00:03:02.963 --> 00:03:04.112
At the top of every module page,

58
00:03:04.112 --> 00:03:09.409
a bar must say Auto-save is ON in green
each time you sit down to work.

59
00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:13.495
If it is red, click the button on the bar
to fix it before you start.

60
00:03:13.495 --> 00:03:17.379
Do not clear your browser data until you
have uploaded your Word file.

61
00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:18.957
Now, deadlines.

62
00:03:18.957 --> 00:03:22.686
Module work is due at 11:59 pm Central on
the Sunday after the module ends.

63
00:03:22.686 --> 00:03:25.971
The final board presentation is
due Thursday, May 13.

64
00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:28.833
Late work is not accepted, so
please plan ahead.

65
00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:32.269
You are welcome to work ahead of schedule.

66
00:03:32.286 --> 00:03:33.503
A word about AI and your grades.

67
00:03:33.503 --> 00:03:36.155
To be transparent, your work is
graded with AI assistance.

68
00:03:36.155 --> 00:03:41.963
It is done by a system my AI team and I
designed that grades against the rubric,

69
00:03:41.963 --> 00:03:44.124
and I review the results.

70
00:03:44.124 --> 00:03:44.724
The AI never posts grades.

71
00:03:44.124 --> 00:03:46.565
If you ever want to discuss a
grade, just ask.

72
00:03:46.565 --> 00:03:49.666
Ethics runs through every module.

73
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:54.465
We use the American College of Healthcare
Executives Code of Ethics.

74
00:03:54.465 --> 00:03:59.236
Everything in this course is fictional, and
you should never put real patient,

75
00:03:59.236 --> 00:04:01.984
employee, or organization
information into an AI tool.

76
00:04:01.984 --> 00:04:05.689
If you have questions, email me at
trinkle at iastate dot edu.

77
00:04:05.689 --> 00:04:09.681
My student hours are Tuesdays from 9:30 to
10:30 in the morning, online,

78
00:04:09.681 --> 00:04:12.264
and the link is in the syllabus.

79
00:04:12.264 --> 00:04:16.426
To get started, open the Start Here
module, and then Module 1.

80
00:04:16.426 --> 00:04:19.200
I am looking forward to working with you.
